The simple MIN_TO_SLOPE > 4.0 would reject the genuine 72→73 (|to_slope|=2.06) — a verified real catch-throw. So my proposed threshold is too aggressive. I need a different slope-based discriminator.

A better one: the product of |from_slope| and |to_slope|, or the geometric mean. Let me check:
- 3→9 (FALSE): 23.59 * 24.34 = 574
- 11→14 (REAL): 4.97 * 21.75 = 108
- 52→54 (REAL): 12.18 * 12.00 = 146
- 68→71 (REAL): 22.00 * 18.08 = 398
