Wait — tracklet 15 is 247 points long, ending at f=595! And the link says from_frame=595 and to_frame=606. The tracklet doesn't end at 595 in a small track — it's a 247-point track that ENDS at f=595. And tracklet 25 STARTS at f=606.

The slopes are computed from the last 5 points of tracklet 15 (end_samples=5) and the first 5 points of tracklet 25 (start_samples=5). The end_slope=-2.076 means the last 5 points of tracklet 15 are barely moving (only 2 px/frame toward the hand). The start_slope=8.773 means the first 5 points of tracklet 25 are moving away from the hand at 8.7 px/frame.

For a real catch-throw, the ball should be decelerating as it approaches the hand (slope becomes less negative near the end) and accelerating as it leaves the hand (slope becomes more positive away from the start). A "pass-through" would have roughly constant velocity through the hand region.

