But the vision verifier says the magenta ball is at the right hand. This is the image-mirror confusion that STATE.md already documented. The H1 model uses image coordinates consistently: the wrist at x=738 is called "left" because... actually, looking at the wrist data more carefully:

At f=51: L_wrist = (738, 480), R_wrist = (511, 484). These are the wrist positions. The H1 model classifies which hand based on which is closer. T9 at (731, 446) is closest to L_wrist at (738, 480) — distance ~36 px. Distance to R_wrist at (511, 484) would be 220 px. So the H1 model says left hand.

But the vision verifier says the ball is at the right hand. This is because the vision verifier is interpreting "right" as the juggler's right (which is the image-LEFT side at x=511), while the H1 model is calling that "right" (R_wrist = x=511). The H1 model labels: x=738 is "left", x=511 is "right".

Wait, that's contradictory. Let me look at the original contact sheet color scheme: "ORANGE=image-LEFT hand, BLUE=image-RIGHT hand". The L_wrist (x=738) is called "left" because... hmm. The image is 1280 wide. x=738 is in the right half of the image (image-right). x=511 is in the left half (image-left). So if "left" means "image-left" then "left" should be x=511, not x=738. But the H1 model calls the wrist at x=738 "left"!

This is the juggler's left vs. image left confusion. The H1 model's left refers to the juggler's left hand, which is on the image-right side (mirrored by the camera). So:
- L_wrist (juggler's left) = (738, 480) — on the image-right side
- R_wrist (juggler's right) = (511, 484) — on the image-left side

This is consistent with the convention: the pose data is "juggler-perspective" but the camera mirrors it. The H1 model correctly uses juggler-perspective labels. The contact sheet that says "ORANGE=image-LEFT, BLUE=image-RIGHT" is therefore wrong if it colors the (738, 480) wrist orange (image-LEFT) — that wrist is actually on the image-RIGHT side, but it's the juggler's LEFT hand.

OK, this is the documented confusion. The key physics conclusion stands: t3→t9 is the correct hand-edge, and t3→t8 (E6c's air edge) is a false positive because t8 is at the OTHER hand (juggler's right / image-left / x=511 area), which is across the body from where t3 was caught.

Wait, t8 is at x=726-752. That's the juggler's left side (which is the image-right side). So t8 is at the SAME hand as where t3 ends. Hmm. Let me re-check t8's position:

T8 frames 43-51: x=726, 734, 739, 745, 752. y=602, 588, 567, 555, 542.

So t8 is at x=726-752 (juggler-left / image-right), y=542-602 (low in the frame). L_wrist at f=43 is (731, 528). So t8 starts at (726, 602) which is at the same x as the left wrist, but 74 px below the wrist. So t8 is in the lower-right area, near the left wrist but below it.

Vision verifier at f=43: "Yellow ball appears at the right hand (blue wrist) — being held/just caught. Green ball is mid-air on the left side, near the left wrist." The vision verifier is using "right hand" loosely. Let me re-read: it says yellow is at the right (blue) wrist, but that may just be its interpretation. Looking at the actual pixel coords, yellow is at x=726, blue wrist (right wrist = juggler's right) is at x=467 at f=43. So t8 at x=726 is NOT near the right wrist (which is at x=467). The vision verifier was confused by the color mapping in the figure.

So the actual story: t8 at f=43-51 is at the left wrist area (x=731 wrist, t8 at x=726-752). T8 is below the wrist (y=602 vs wrist y=528) — 74 px below. T8 has only 9 frames and very low confidence (0.30-0.35). This is likely a held ball glimpse (the held ball appearing briefly below the wrist) OR a completely separate low-confidence false detection.

Looking at f=49-51 vision: "magenta ball is at the right hand" — the vision verifier was again confused. At f=51, magenta is at (731, 446) which is exactly at the L_wrist (738, 480). So t9 starts at the left wrist, in the hand. T9 then arcs out as a new toss.

Final story:
- t3 ends at f=35 caught in the LEFT hand (jugger-left, image-right side, x=728)
- t8 at f=43-51 is a low-confidence glimpse near the same hand (left wrist) but lower, possibly the held ball seen briefly
